<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Rahman I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/731">731</a>–788 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd al-Rahman I was an Umayyad prince who escaped the massacre of his family during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution">Abbasid Revolution</a> and fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. In 756 he established an independent Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, which never recognised Abbasid authority. His survival meant that Umayyad rule continued in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> in the east, limiting the reach of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> in the west.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-i.jpg" alt="Abd al-Rahman I" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_abd_al_rahman_i_21816.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
